# Signal Angular v22+ ONLY Frontend Rules (`web/**`)

Deep references: `docs/engineering/ANGULAR_ENGINEERING_GUIDE.md`, `docs/engineering/ANGULAR_UI_STYLE_GUIDE.md` | Skills: `signal-angular-workbench`, `signal-angular-ui-style-system`, `signal-zero-leak-canvas-and-dlp`, `signal-universal-parts-registry`, `signal-cad-cam-plm-ops`, `signal-collab-and-status-reviews`, `signal-release-deploy-topology`.

## 1. Mandatory Stack Floor & Modern Angular v22+ Separation (Zero Inline Templates/Styles)
- **Strict Minimum Toolchain (`web/`):** **Angular `v22+` ONLY** (`>= 22.0.0`), **TypeScript `6.0+`** (strict), **Node.js `26 LTS+`** (`>= 26.13.0` for CLI & Tier 1 SSR/CSP-nonce edge ONLY), and **`pnpm 11+`** (`ignore-scripts` default). Reject any Angular `< 22`, `Zone.js`, or legacy `NgModule` dependency!
- Standalone Components ONLY, `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` (Angular v22 default), **Zoneless** reactivity (`signal`, `computed`, `linkedSignal`, `effect`), and **Stable Signal Forms**.
- Use signal APIs (`input()`, `input.required()`, `output()`, `model()`, `viewChild()`) and function-based `inject()` — NEVER `@Input()`, `@Output()`, `@ViewChild()`, or constructor DI parameter lists.
- Use built-in template control flow (`@if`, `@for (...; track item.id)`, `@switch`, `@defer`) — NEVER `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`.
- **Mandatory Separate Files Per Component (NEVER inline `template:` or `styles:`):**
  - `<name>.component.ts` (`<= 120 LOC`): thin Angular glue (`templateUrl`, inputs/outputs, `vm = computed(...)`, event delegation).
  - `<name>.component.html` (`<= 150 LOC`): pure flat declarative markup bound ONLY to `vm()` properties and `@signal/ui-kit`.
  - `<name>.logic.ts` (`<= 250 LOC`): pure framework-agnostic TS owning ALL branching, status/badge lookup maps, role/profile filtering, formatting, and config arrays (tested without TestBed in `.logic.spec.ts`!).
  - `<name>.model.ts`: `readonly` view-models, config types, and `bigint` SI DTOs.
- Keep RxJS strictly at async transport/stream edges (`toSignal`, `takeUntilDestroyed`); never leak manual `.subscribe()` calls.

## 2. Anti-Spaghetti HTML Laws & Centralized Style Ecosystem (Zero Per-Component Styles!)
- **No `@if` Soup & Zero Copy-Pasted Sections:** Never write compound boolean expressions (`&&`/`||`/role checks) in HTML, never nest control flow deeper than `2` levels, NEVER duplicate HTML cards/forms/toolbars across `@if`/`@else` branches (drive variants via `.logic.ts` config arrays & `@for`), and extract any branch `> 15` HTML lines into a pure `ui/` or `@signal/ui-kit` component!
- **Centralized Styles ONLY (`@signal/design-system` + `@signal/ui-kit`):** Feature/workbench components MUST NOT create `.component.css`/`.scss` files, inline `styles: [...]`, or HTML `style="..."`! Reuse global tokens/primitives (`.sig-*` in `web/libs/design-system`) and standardized HTML components (`sig-*` in `web/libs/ui-kit`) across the entire platform.
- **Rare Style Exception Gate:** Only genuinely specialized visual geometry (e.g., radial pie-menu trigonometry, canvas crosshair reticle) may declare `styleUrl`, requiring line-1 `/* @sig-style-exception: <reason> */`, `<= 60 LOC`, 100% `var(--sig-*)` tokens (zero raw hex/px), zero `::ng-deep`, and zero `!important`.
- Respect `web/libs/<domain>/src/index.ts` as the sole public barrel; coordinate cross-pane highlights via `@signal/workspace-bus`; lazy-load all 23 workbenches so initial shell stays `< 250 KB` gzipped; use `cdk-virtual-scroll` for lists/grids `> 50` rows.

## 3. 64-Bit `bigint` Precision & Engineering UX
- ALL 64-bit integer contract fields (`_nm`, `_ps`, `_fs`, `fencing_epoch`, `provider_repo_id`) MUST remain ES2020 `bigint` (`longAsBigint: true`). **NEVER** cast them to JS `number` (`Number(x)`).
- Always render explicit SI unit confirmation pills (`sig-si-unit-input` / `.sig-si-pill`) distinguishing `m` (`milli`) from `Meg` (`mega`) with tabular monospace `.sig-mono`.
- Comply with WCAG 2.2 AA: Okabe-Ito color-blind-safe tokens + procedural stipple patterns, keyboard-only CAD wiring/navigation, and ARIA live announcements.
- Keep context URL-scoped (`/org/:org_slug/project/:proj_slug/*`) — never store active org/project in global singleton state.

## 4. Zero-Leak Viewport, DLP & XSS Guardrails
- **NEVER** store design IP, netlists, layouts, waveforms, specs, or firmware in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, `IndexedDB`, Service Worker caches, or downloadable Blob URLs. Reconnect buffers (`<= 60 s`) live strictly in a volatile JS RAM closure.
- Under Enterprise Zero-Leak mode, never buffer raw geometry in JS; render interactive HUD widgets via `HudOverlayPrimitive` over `signal-render`'s Dual-Plane `Zstd-QOI`/WebP + hardware video GPU Atlas. Multi-Monitor pop-outs use same-origin volatile `BroadcastChannel` + inherited focus curtains & watermarks.
- **NEVER** use `bypassSecurityTrust*`, `innerHTML`, `eval`, `new Function`, or `window.print()`. Preserve CSP nonces, Trusted Types, and Route-Partitioned `COOP`/`COEP`.

## 5. Verification Before Commit
Run `pnpm --filter @signal/web lint`, `pnpm --filter @signal/web typecheck`, `pnpm --filter @signal/web test --run`, and `pnpm audit --ignore-scripts`.

## 6. Dev Response & Anti-Hallucination
Reply in **2–3 sentences max** (`Issue -> Fix -> Observed check result`). Verify Angular `v22+`/`package.json` APIs and file paths via `rg`/`view_file` before editing; never claim green without observed exit code `0`.
